file tools/g/glow_ident_witness.rish the gate, quoting each named leg so a leg that breaks is heard
file tools/fixtures/g/glow_ceiling_refusal_scan.sh ceiling 40 to 34, and the blind spot the fall exposed
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri glow_ident rostered at lap tier beside its sibling
scope one bounded language change: the Zig-identifier rule published once, a six-module cohort converted with its own six guards GREEN, the remaining 23 copies metered under a falling ceiling, and the sibling meter's own blind spot named where its readers will meet it
obs Four cold reds stood at this lap's open and all four closed. Two were mine: shell_dialect and its pre-commit twin read two sed -i sites against a ceiling of zero, both written into my own control to swap a ceiling, and the portable form reads to a new file and writes back through the original. One was mine at one remove -- fold_shelf_link_repoint named three depth-lost links, the first of them my own last lap's shelved account pointing at my own control file. The fourth was the day rolling over: session-logs/README.md and CHAPTERS.md both still carried 20260916 open while the 20260917 shelf already held a log, so the count was derived off the shelf's own rows rather than typed, 93 in both rosters, and session_roster_agree holds them to that one reading.
obs The gated sed -i is the lap's cheapest lesson and the one most worth keeping: the pre-commit hook would have refused the commit, so the wall worked, and the cold endurance run is what let me meet it while the repair still cost one edit rather than a rejected send.
obs The hot scoped endurance run named seventeen reds and exactly one was mine, which is the lap's sharpest finding about its own instruments. glow_refusal reddened on the sentence assert selftest.out contains "16 legs, 0 failures" -- a RECITED leg tally, reddening the moment five legs arrived. Its own sibling glow_ceiling_refusal_witness.rish carries a header paragraph stating the opposite discipline by name: a recited total reds on the lap somebody adds a leg, which teaches a lane to stop adding them. Two guards one room apart, one stating the rule and one breaking it.
obs The repair takes the sibling's shape rather than bumping the number: each of the five new legs is asserted by name, and the tally line becomes 0 failures -- GREEN alone. So a leg that BREAKS is still heard and a leg that ARRIVES is not punished, which is the whole distinction the sibling draws. My own new witness was written to that rule already, which is why it reads GREEN beside a sibling that did not.
obs The other sixteen were checked one at a time against my own paths rather than assumed inherited: instrument_refusal names two peer files landed at the commit this lap opened on; unheard_guard lists twenty controls and mine is not among them, since my witness runs it; error_member_reach names ten dead members in ten files, none of which I touched; ratchet_slack names one uncompared ceiling, awk_lcg_exact, while both of mine read compared=yes with zero slack; shim_reason, say_compose_bound, shared_build_path and pen_release return zero hits for my paths. built_tool_freshness reads the rye binary behind rye/src/main.rye, which a peer is holding open on the claim board.
status GREEN -- glow_ident (16 pen legs, 2 mutations bitten), glow_refusal (21 legs, its recited tally derived), glow_ceiling_refusal, glow_desk_run (347 desks), glow_expr, and the six converted modules' own guards all GREEN on metal; tame_style_check, width_check, opening_lines, ascii_document, link_text_promise, log_has_a_row, session_roster_agree, index_row_bound, shell_dialect, shell_dialect_touch and fold_shelf_link_repoint GREEN after the four cold reds closed
recommend keep-going -- the next fall the copy meter can name is the four lower_compose_core siblings, which share one ceiling and convert as one cohort
